# Git commits

- Author and committer are always **Ravi Ranjan <raviranjan.amu@gmail.com>**.
- Never mention AI, Cursor, agent, assistant, bot or any model name in commit messages, tags, branch names, PR titles/descriptions or code comments.
- No `Co-authored-by:`, `Generated-by:` or similar trailers. Ravi Ranjan is the only author.

Commit like this:

```bash
git -c user.name="Ravi Ranjan" -c user.email="raviranjan.amu@gmail.com" \
  commit --author="Ravi Ranjan <raviranjan.amu@gmail.com>" -m "Add fee receipt printing"
```

Before pushing, check and amend if anything else appears:

```bash
git log -1 --format="%an <%ae> | %cn <%ce>%n%B"
```

```text
BAD : "Add login page (generated with Cursor)"  /  "Co-authored-by: Cursor Agent"
GOOD: "Add a single Login button that opens school.ranjanravi.com"
```